<SddDiscoverFromCode keywords="discover, from-code, reverse-engineer, brownfield, recover-specs, general-picture, understanding-block, incremental, lazy, align-code, sdd-discover-from-code" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Recover the GENERAL PICTURE of an existing codebase as SDD specs — project-scale, brownfield.
    Entered from `root` when the portal is absent but `sdd-state --probe` reports `CODE=present`: the
    repo already holds code, so we do not invent a vision over it — we read what is there and formalize
    the big picture first. Loaded by `root` (which runs only after the router); the router-core beliefs it
    relies on are declared in `BeliefState deps` (inherited, not repeated).

    The primary deliverable is the portal: an operator-confirmed Vision + Scope Graph + a recovered infra
    scope. That is a complete, valid outcome on its own. Deep elaboration — module specs, rule extraction,
    contract/style alignment tasks — is INCREMENTAL: done per scope, only when the operator asks to go
    deeper, with the flow loading spec-elaboration only for that part. We recover the map first; we do not
    recover the whole repo at once, and we do not overload the operator.

    Key interaction rule: the vision is not fully in the code, so the agent does not ask the operator to
    supply it from scratch — it presents what it understood (coarse first, marking how confident it is in
    each item) and the operator agrees, augments, or corrects in free text. This is a review, not a
    multiple-choice question.

    Reuses the branches — portal via the portal format, infra via `infra`, modules via `module`, tasks
    via `scaffold`; it does NOT re-enter `root` (which routed here — re-entry would loop). Distinct from
    `reconcile-from-code` (one change/module against an existing spec triangle).
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_TOOL_INVOCATION, AX_OPERATOR_DIALOGUE_STYLE, AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION, AX_OPERATOR_OUTPUT_LIVE_TEXT">
    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-evidence-hygiene"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <KernelGrammar>
    {{> "definition/process/def-read-and-use-directive"}}
  </KernelGrammar>

  <ChatProtocol>
    {{> "contract/process/halt-format"}}
  </ChatProtocol>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_CODE` | `sdd-state --probe` reports `CODE=absent` — wrong branch; return to `root` greenfield init |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejects the recovered picture outright — stop; nothing is written |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_CARTOGRAPHY">
      <Goal>Read the COARSE picture — cheap, write nothing.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From `sdd-state --probe` (`code-dirs`, `configs`) + a coarse read — `package.json` (name,
        workspaces, deps), entry points, top-level layout — infer **candidate scopes** (workspace
        packages, else top-level domain dirs) and a rough module list, the toolchain, and a light read of
        conventions + a contract signal. Do NOT deep-read every module; the goal here is the map, not the
        detail. Read-only.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_PICTURE">
      <Goal>Show the general picture; let the operator steer.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present the **general picture** (`UNDERSTANDING_BLOCK_FORMAT`), plain Russian, coarse first:
        inferred **vision** (what the code does — but marked operator-owned: «зачем и куда — твоё»),
        the **scope graph**, the **infra/toolchain**, and a short note on conventions + contract state.
        Mark **confidence** per item — read-for-sure vs guessed vs «не смог отнести к scope/модулю, реши
        ты» — and steer the operator's attention to the unsure spots. Frame: «вот общая картина как я
        понял — согласись, дополни, поправь». Open free-text — NOT a multiple-choice question.
        Fold corrections into the locked picture. Outright rejection → `H_OPERATOR_REJECT`. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_PERSIST_PICTURE">
      <Goal>Persist the picture — the primary, self-sufficient outcome.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Assemble the portal (Vision + Scope Graph + Scopes table) directly via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/portal-structure.xml")` — do NOT re-enter
        `root` (it routed here — re-entry would loop). Recover the infra scope from the configs via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/infra.directive.xml")`. The repo now has a portal —
        a valid place to stop.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_DEEPEN">
      <Goal>Go deeper — by parts, only what the operator picks (optional, incremental).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Offer to elaborate; the picture already stands, so this is opt-in and incremental. For each
        scope the operator chooses: recover its module specs via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml")` (behavioral truth — what the
        code does); record the de-facto rules + the contract gap; and, when the operator wants the code
        aligned, scaffold **behavior-preserving** alignment tasks via
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scaffold.directive.xml")` — prioritized, not one per
        gap (contract alignment on pre-DbC code is a large effort — scope it). Loop per chosen scope; the
        operator can stop anytime. Load these branches only for the part being deepened.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Prove what was produced is coherent.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Whatever exists now (at minimum portal + infra; plus any deepened scopes) is coherent;
        `sdd-check --all` clean. Return control.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    Service line — dim, internal, never narrated (`AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`):
    `🧭 DFC_R<N> · scopes=<n> · deepened=<n> · step=<id>`.

    {{> "contract/process/understanding-block-format"}}

    {{> "contract/process/message-layout"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-progressive-disclosure"}}
  </ChatOutput>
</SddDiscoverFromCode>
